240   C  TITL$NUCLEAR STRUCTURE AND DECAY DATA FOR A=240                        
240   c  AUTH$C. Morse                                                          
240   c  INST$National Nuclear Data Center                                      
240  #c       Brookhaven National Laboratory,                                   
240  #c       Upton, New York 11973-5000, USA                                   
240   C  CIT$NDS 206, 359 (2025)                                                
240   c  ABST$The experimental reaction and decay studies producing nuclei in   
240  2c  the A=240 mass chain have been reviewed.  Data on elements from        
240  3c  uranium (Z=92) to einsteinium (Z=99) are included, and level and decay 
240  4c  schemes are presented for these nuclides.  This work supersedes the    
240  4c  previous evaluation for this mass chain (2008Si25).                    
240   c  CUT$All literature available up to September 27, 2024 has been         
240  2c  considered. The NSR database (2014Pr09) was the main bibliographic     
240  3c  source: www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr                                           
240   c  ACKN$This material is based on work supported by the U.S. Department   
240  2c  of Energy, Office of Science, Office of Nuclear Physics under Contract 
240  3c  No.  |DE-AC02-98CH10946.  The evaluator is grateful to the compilers   
240  4c  of the XUNDL database for their compilation of the relevant datasets,  
240  5c  and to Catherine-Anne Dunn (NNDC, BNL) for providing access to some of 
240  6c  the material referenced in the evaluation.  This work also benefited   
240  7c  from the previous evaluation of the A=240 isotopes (2008Si25).         

