240PU cB IB$The |b feedings are poorly known for most levels since the          
240PU2cB multipolarities and mixing ratios of |g-ray transitions are not well   
240PU3cB established, thus all feedings, except that for 1309 keV level are     
240PU4cB treated as uncertain and given mostly without uncertainties. From K|p  
240PU5cB assignments, only the strong feeding to the topmost level at 1309 keV  
240PU6cB is definite with |DK=0. All other feedings are less likely since       
240PU7cB these involve a high degree of K-forbiddenness with |DK=2 to 5.        
240PU8cB Apparent large intensity imbalances for some of the levels suggests    
240PU9cB that the decay scheme is incomplete.                                   
