240PU c  Includes {+238}U(|a,F) from 1997Er09                                   
240PU c  2001Ga05, 2001Th16, 2000Pa40 (also 2001Kr05): E=25 MeV.  Measured      
240PU2c  E|g, I|g, |g|g using six Ge CLUSTERS, each cluster with four Ge        
240PU3c  detectors of the EUROBALL array; ce data; Gamma- and ce-spectroscopy   
240PU4c  in the superdeformed minimum of {+240}Pu                               
240PU c  1972Sp06: E=25 MeV, transitions in second minimum studied with iron-   
240PU2c  free spectrometer in coincidence with delayed fission fragments;       
240PU3c  transitions in the g.s. band studied in ce singles and |g-ce           
240PU4c  coincidence.                                                           
240PU c  1997Er09: {+238}U(|a,F) E=20.0-31.2 MeV. Measured fission T{-1/2}.     
240PU2c  Deduced second potential (superdeformed) well depth.                   
240PU c  Other: 1973Be10                                                        
240PU c  Data for excited superdeformed bands are from 2001Ga05, 2001Th16 and   
240PU2c  2000Pa40 (all from the same laboratory). In a few cases where          
240PU3c  corresponding values differ somewhat between these three papers,       
240PU4c  those from 2001Ga05 (being the latest paper) are adopted here. Some    
240PU5c  levels are listed only in 2001Th16. Data for the g.s. SD band are      
240PU6c  from 1972Sp06                                                          
240PU cG $Other electron lines, assigned as E0, are seen at 280.3 (1.7%),       
240PU2cG 289.7 (2.3%) and 296.0 (1.0%), which correspond to transition          
240PU3cG energies near 411 keV (2001Ga05). These transitions probably define    
240PU4cG other K|p=1- bands. In 2001Th16, there are tentative transitions of    
240PU5cG energies: 410.5, 414.2 and 420 with dominant E0 component.             
240PU cG E$From 2001Ga05 for transitions in the second minimum, unless          
240PU2cG otherwise stated                                                       
240PU cG E(D)$From Adopted Gammas                                               
240PU cG E(E)$From 1983Ha31                                                     
240PU cG E(F)$From 1972Sp06                                                     
240PU cG E(T)$Tentative transition from 2001Th16 only                           
240PU cG E(A)$Transition seen in ce data (2001Ga05). Absolute K-shell           
240PU2cG intensity, if available, is given under comments                       
240PU cG M$Based on |a(L2), |a(L3), |a(M2), |a(M3) data of 1972Sp06 for |g's    
240PU2cG of second minimum. The ground-state band multipolarities are taken     
240PU3cG from 1983Ha31. The E0 assignment is from ce data of 2001Ga05 and       
240PU4cG 2001Th16. Except for the 769.9 (0+ to 0+) transition, all other        
240PU5cG transitions are likely to have M1+E2 components; these assignments     
240PU6cG are in parentheses since conversion coefficients are not available     
240PU cG RI$For SD bands, intensities are per 100 fissions of the isomer        
240PU2cG (2001Ga05,2001Th16). For transitions in SD bands where dominant decay  
240PU3cG seems to be through E0, absolute K-shell intensities                   
240PU4cG (2001Ga05,2001Th16) are given under comments. The transition           
240PU5cG intensities in these cases will be |?1.2 times the K-shell intensity   
240PU6cG and undetected photon intensity for |DJ=1 transitions. Normalization   
240PU7cG is based on the number of delayed fission events                       
240PU cL $Lifetime estimates for some of the bandheads are listed by 2001Ga05   
240PU2cL and 2001Th16, these are based on systematics, not on lifetime          
240PU3cL measurements.                                                          
240PU cL E$For SD bands values are from 2001Ga05 when available; otherwise      
240PU2cL from 2001Th16. For the normal g.s. band, values are from E|g's         
240PU cL J$From Adopted Levels for g.s. band. From 2001Ga05 for SD bands. In    
240PU2cL Adopted Levels, all assignments for SD band levels are given in        
240PU3cL parentheses due to lack of strong supporting arguments.                
240PU cL E(X)$x=2250 {I200}, deduced from the level density of K|p=0+           
240PU2cL bandheads in {+239}Pu(d,pF) (2001Hu12,2001Th16). Other: 2800 {I200}    
240PU3cL (estimate by 1971Br39,1970Bu02,1973Na03)                               
