240PU    239PU(D,PF)                   2001HU12                  25NDS    202511
240PU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C. Morse$CIT=NDS 206, 359 (2025)$CUT=27-Sep-2024$          
240PU c  2001Hu12 (also 1999Hu12,2001Th16): E=12.5 MeV. Measured protons in     
240PU2c  coin with the fission fragments. FWHM=7 keV for proton spectrum.       
240PU3c  Deduced several rotational and vibrational bands in the second         
240PU4c  minimum of the potential well from the analysis of the proton          
240PU5c  spectrum in the excitation region of 3.8-5.6 MeV.                      
240PU c  2003Ni01: E=13.5 MeV. Protons measured with |DE-E telescope silicon    
240PU2c  detectors. The fission fragments were detected in coin mode with two   
240PU3c  silicon PIN diodes. FWHM(proton spectrum)=55 keV. Measured             
240PU4c  proton-fission fragment coin; mass distribution of {+240}Pu fission    
240PU5c  fragments following the |b-vibrational resonance at 5.1 MeV in the     
240PU6c  second minimum of the double-humped fission barrier                    
240PU c  Earlier (d,pF) studies: 1976Go13, 1976Gl01, 1971Ba30, 1969Pe07,        
240PU2c  1969La14, 1968Br32, 1965Br40.                                          
240PU c  Two vibrational resonance groups centered at 4.6 MeV and 5.1 MeV       
240PU2c  excitation energy were observed and attributed to 3-phonon and         
240PU3c  4-phonon |b-vibrational states. Each group was further resolved into   
240PU4c  several substates which could be assigned as the low-spin members of   
240PU5c  K|p=0+ SD rotational bands on the basis of regular pattern of triplet  
240PU6c  (0+, 2+ and 4+) of states for each substructure                        
240PU cL E$x=energy of the g.s. in the second minimum (3.6-ns fission isomer)   
240PU2cL is deduced as 2250 {I200} from the resonance structure.                
240PU cL E(A),J(A)$Probable bandheads of 3-phonon |b-vibration (2001Hu12) in    
240PU2cL the second minimum. The structure shows a picket-fence type pattern    
240PU3cL of possibly the 0+, 2+ and 4+ states of the SD rotational band         
240PU cL E(B)$Attributed to 4-phonon |b-vibration (2001Hu12) in the second      
240PU2cL minimum. This resonance may be composed of 13 rotational bands as      
240PU3cL shown in the fit of the proton spectrum. See also 2003Ni01 for mass    
240PU4cL distribution measurements                                              
