240PU    COULOMB EXCITATION            2007WAZV,1974MC15,1973BE4425NDS    202511
240PU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C. Morse$CIT=NDS 206, 359 (2025)$CUT=27-Sep-2024$          
240PU c  1998Ha08 (also 1999Wi11,1999Cl07): ({+208}Pb,{+208}Pb') E=1300 MeV.    
240PU2c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g using the Argonne-Notre Dame array of 12       
240PU3c  Compton-suppressed Ge detectors and 46 BGO scintillators. Enriched     
240PU4c  (98%) target. 1999Wi11 report measurements with GAMMASPHERE array      
240PU5c  containing 101 Ge detectors. The experiments reported by 1998Ha08,     
240PU6c  1999Wi11 and 1999Cl07 are by the same experimental group as 2007WaZV,  
240PU7c  where most data details are given                                      
240PU c  2007WaZV, 2009Wa04, 2011Ca35: ({+208}Pb,{+208}Pb'), E=1300 MeV.        
240PU2c  Target={+240}Pu. Experiment performed at ATLAS-Argonne facility using  
240PU3c  Gammasphere array with 99 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors. Measured    
240PU4c  E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g(|q). The beam energy is 10-15% above the Coulomb    
240PU5c  barrier, thus the method is called 'unsafe' Coulomb excitation. The    
240PU6c  results from this experiment were also reported at NS-2008 conference  
240PU7c  at NSCL, Michigan in June 2008                                         
240PU c  1974Mc15, 1973Be44, 1971Fo17: (|a,|a') E=17 MeV. Measured B(E2)'s.     
240PU2c  The |a spectrum is shown in 1973Be44                                   
240PU c  1965Fr11: (d,d')                                                       
240PU c  All data given here are from 2007WaZV, unless otherwise stated         
240PU cG $A |g-ray cascade: 303.5-340.3-370.7-405.8-437.5-466.8 possibly        
240PU2cG belongs to {+240}Pu (2007WaZV)                                         
240PU cG M$Assigned on the basis of A{-2} and A{-4} coefficients from           
240PU2cG 2007WaZV. The mult=Q most likely corresponds to E2 and mult=D to E1    
240PU cL $A level at 938,(2+) with B(E2)=0.079 {I18} (1974Mc15,1973Be44) is     
240PU2cL omitted here. First the 938 level in other reactions (see 'adopted     
240PU3cL levels') is assigned 1-; second from the spectrum figure in 1973Be44,  
240PU4cL the peak corresponding to 938 is very weak and, assuming a linear      
