240PU    240AM EC DECAY                1972AH07,1971LEZO,1972POZS25NDS    202511
240PU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C. Morse$CIT=NDS 206, 359 (2025)$CUT=27-Sep-2024$          
240PU c  1972Ah07: Measured E|g, I|g, ce, (ce)(|g) coin, mass-separated         
240PU2c  source, Ge(Li) and Si(Li) detectors. Source prepared by                
240PU3c  {+237}Np(|a,n) reaction at 30 MeV. Subsequent to chemical separation   
240PU4c  the source was run through the Argonne isotope separator to obtain     
240PU5c  enriched {+240}Am samples. A total of 14 |g rays were reported: 42.9,  
240PU6c  98.9 and 12 |g rays from 888 to 1295 keV. In the level scheme, eight   
240PU7c  |g rays were assigned amongst five excited states. Conversion          
240PU8c  electron intensities were given in percent per {+240}Am decay, but no  
240PU9c  uncertainties were quoted in these intensities and the procedure to    
240PUac  normalize ce intensities to |g-ray intensities was not explained.      
240PU c  1971LeZO: Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, ce, chemically separated source,    
240PU2c  Ge(Li) detectors singles and Compton-suppressed, Si(Li) electron       
240PU3c  spectrometer, (x ray)|g coin using two NaI(Tl) detectors. A total of   
240PU4c  31 |g rays and two conversion lines (for 42.9|g and 99.0|g) reported.  
240PU5c  Full experimental details about normalization of electron spectra and  
240PU6c  spectral (|g and ce) figures are not available in this report.         
240PU c  1972PoZS: Measured E|g, I|g, half-life, chemically separated source    
240PU2c  prepared by {+237}Np(|a,n) reaction at 50 MeV. Ge(Li) detector used.   
240PU3c  A total of 23 |g rays reported between 305 and 1296 keV. Small         
240PU4c  impurities of {+140}La, {+143}Ce and {+239}Am were present in the      
240PU5c  source. Twenty |g rays were placed in a level scheme essentially       
240PU6c  based on the one from 1971LeZO. No uncertainties were quoted on        
