240ES cL CONF$From systematics of Es (Z=99) isotopes, |p7/2[633] (i{-13/2})     
240ES2cL and |p3/2[521] (f{-7/2}) orbitals are expected near the proton Fermi   
240ES3cL surface, while the |n5/2[633] (g{-9/2}) orbital is expected near the   
240ES4cL neutron Fermi surface for N=141 isotones. Thus, using the              
240ES5cL Gallagher-Moszkowski rule, one may expect K|p=1+,                      
240ES6cL |p7/2[633]~#|n5/2[633] for the ground state and K|p=6+,                
240ES7cL |p7/2[633]~#|n5/2[633] for an excited isomeric state. K|p=1-,          
240ES8cL |p3/2[521]~#|n5/2[633] is a possible alternative. The assignments are  
240ES9cL tentative                                                              

